01:03:11.848 --> 01:03:14.500
But it's really the second
half of the documentary,

01:03:14.500 --> 01:03:16.750
wouldn't you agree where
it really starts to sing?

01:03:16.750 --> 01:03:19.570
Like once they achieve their initial fame,

01:03:19.570 --> 01:03:20.500
and then,

01:03:20.500 --> 01:03:22.573
I just related to it so much from a,

01:03:24.640 --> 01:03:27.810
from a creative standpoint,
like working closely

01:03:27.810 --> 01:03:29.970
with a lifelong friend of mine

01:03:29.970 --> 01:03:31.903
and having to,

01:03:33.105 --> 01:03:36.450
having to pivot from early successes

01:03:36.450 --> 01:03:39.230
to find later successes in their career.

01:03:39.230 --> 01:03:41.450
And just the,

01:03:41.450 --> 01:03:44.840
it was very inspiring to me because

01:03:44.840 --> 01:03:46.350
I related to so much of it.

01:03:46.350 --> 01:03:47.420
Yeah. I thought it was great.

01:03:47.420 --> 01:03:50.160
I mean, I, I didn't know,

01:03:50.160 --> 01:03:51.910
I knew so little about them.

01:03:51.910 --> 01:03:53.010
And the thing we talked about

01:03:53.010 --> 01:03:56.380
is we were trying to figure out
why we weren't more of a fan

01:03:56.380 --> 01:03:57.560
All along the way. Yeah.

01:03:57.560 --> 01:03:58.850
Like, especially like in the nineties

01:03:58.850 --> 01:03:59.683
when we were in high school,

01:03:59.683 --> 01:04:03.130
because we were like
listening to 311 and I mean,

01:04:03.130 --> 01:04:05.550
311 is no Beastie Boys.

01:04:05.550 --> 01:04:06.611
You know what I'm saying?

01:04:06.611 --> 01:04:07.444
Yeah.

01:04:07.444 --> 01:04:08.420
It's just interesting that

01:04:08.420 --> 01:04:11.480
that's what we gravitated
towards, but fascinating story.

01:04:11.480 --> 01:04:15.090
Just the way things
worked back in the day,

01:04:15.090 --> 01:04:17.670
in the music industry and the
way things kind of came up

01:04:17.670 --> 01:04:19.810
with like a new genre being invented.

01:04:19.810 --> 01:04:21.800
So I think, I mean, I enjoyed all of it.

01:04:21.800 --> 01:04:23.270
I thought the beginning was awesome too,

01:04:23.270 --> 01:04:26.080
because it's just fascinating to see

01:04:26.080 --> 01:04:29.540
how all that came together
back in the MTV days

01:04:29.540 --> 01:04:31.420
and the way it worked.

01:04:31.420 --> 01:04:32.260
So foreign.

01:04:32.260 --> 01:04:35.513
The thing that I really appreciated was,

01:04:37.098 --> 01:04:40.670
they processed their entire experience

01:04:40.670 --> 01:04:43.070
through a lens of like a maturity

01:04:43.070 --> 01:04:47.840
that they grew into over time. You know?

01:04:47.840 --> 01:04:49.200
They said,

01:04:49.200 --> 01:04:51.840
it's not that we became adults
as much as we kinda just

01:04:51.840 --> 01:04:53.090
gained some maturity, you know,

01:04:53.090 --> 01:04:55.740
In a lot of ways that I don't think in,

01:04:55.740 --> 01:04:57.780
in a way that I relate
to, in a lot of ways

01:04:57.780 --> 01:05:00.760
I don't feel like an adult,
but I feel like I have this,

01:05:00.760 --> 01:05:03.270
I can look back on our
career with like this level

01:05:03.270 --> 01:05:05.223
of maturity and, you know,

01:05:06.540 --> 01:05:09.730
we haven't pivoted as much as they did.

01:05:09.730 --> 01:05:13.890
You know, from this, their
first album and like the

01:05:13.890 --> 01:05:17.280
becoming this, becoming the trope

01:05:17.280 --> 01:05:19.690
that they were making
fun of while on tour,

01:05:19.690 --> 01:05:22.173
like this fight for your
right to party guys,

01:05:23.240 --> 01:05:24.540
and then coming to grips with

01:05:24.540 --> 01:05:26.760
how that wasn't who they truly were.

01:05:26.760 --> 01:05:29.453
I just really enjoyed how
they processed it and,

01:05:30.493 --> 01:05:34.053
and presented it with like
this retrospective wisdom.

01:05:35.750 --> 01:05:38.043
That, I didn't know, I
didn't know was there.

01:05:38.043 --> 01:05:39.853
It's like, you know that Adam Jaak,

01:05:41.202 --> 01:05:43.707
you know, he became this

01:05:45.650 --> 01:05:48.390
crusader for, for Tibet

01:05:49.335 --> 01:05:50.168
and you know,

01:05:50.168 --> 01:05:53.450
he's a fascinating guy
and you get to know him

01:05:53.450 --> 01:05:55.208
through the lens of his, of,

01:05:55.208 --> 01:05:57.650
of his friends talking about him,

01:05:57.650 --> 01:05:59.067
which I thought was really cool too.

01:05:59.067 --> 01:06:00.010
Yeah.

01:06:00.010 --> 01:06:01.440
So it was a great tribute to him.

01:06:01.440 --> 01:06:02.453
It's very moving.

01:06:03.860 --> 01:06:05.390
If you liked the tour Mythicality,

01:06:05.390 --> 01:06:08.166
I think, you know, and if I could see,

01:06:08.166 --> 01:06:13.166
I can see how mythical beasts process us,

01:06:13.850 --> 01:06:17.750
I kind of put myself
in their shoes and it,

01:06:17.750 --> 01:06:18.583
because,

01:06:18.583 --> 01:06:19.500
You put less pressure on.

01:06:19.500 --> 01:06:21.750
In being a fan of the Beastie Boys.

01:06:21.750 --> 01:06:23.080
Performers in that moment,

01:06:23.080 --> 01:06:25.160
because you're kind of
taking in their story.

01:06:25.160 --> 01:06:26.820
Yeah. And I started to,

01:06:26.820 --> 01:06:29.210
I really understood each of them as an,

01:06:29.210 --> 01:06:30.190
as an individual

01:06:30.190 --> 01:06:32.070
and began to understand
their personalities.

01:06:32.070 --> 01:06:33.600
And I felt like I got to know them

01:06:33.600 --> 01:06:35.400
and appreciate who they were.

01:06:35.400 --> 01:06:36.233
And then,

01:06:37.270 --> 01:06:39.210
in going back and
listening to those albums

01:06:39.210 --> 01:06:42.230
that we should have been
into, you're right, before.

01:06:42.230 --> 01:06:44.350
I had this appreciation for the albums,

01:06:44.350 --> 01:06:47.300
because I had an appreciation
for who they were as people

01:06:47.300 --> 01:06:49.260
and the journeys that they had been on.

01:06:49.260 --> 01:06:51.370
And I,

01:06:51.370 --> 01:06:52.460
I feel good that I've,

01:06:52.460 --> 01:06:54.123
that we've given,

01:06:55.250 --> 01:06:57.070
we've given that to Mythical Beast.

01:06:57.070 --> 01:07:00.340
You know? We brought them,
they understand our journey.

01:07:00.340 --> 01:07:03.110
They know us as people,
they know our quirks,

01:07:03.110 --> 01:07:06.040
they know our differences.
They know, they know what,

01:07:06.040 --> 01:07:07.500
what makes us work together.

01:07:07.500 --> 01:07:09.010
And they're pulling for us

01:07:09.010 --> 01:07:13.050
in the way that I was pulling
for them in their story.

01:07:13.050 --> 01:07:16.220
So when, when it seemed like they broke up

01:07:16.220 --> 01:07:19.770
without even talking about it, that was,

01:07:19.770 --> 01:07:20.840
that was a great point.

01:07:20.840 --> 01:07:21.780
Spoiler alert!

01:07:21.780 --> 01:07:23.450
So to see what happened

01:07:23.450 --> 01:07:27.036
from that, in that moment, you know?

01:07:27.036 --> 01:07:28.820
And how they're just, they were,

01:07:28.820 --> 01:07:30.340
they're just real people.

01:07:30.340 --> 01:07:31.173
Yeah.

01:07:31.173 --> 01:07:33.810
And they put it all out there.

01:07:33.810 --> 01:07:34.643
So.

